{
  "requirement": "Where subagents are unavailable, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to review each group themselves against the review prompt of {cite}`requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.review_prompt`, one group at a time, before presenting any group to the user.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The only structural obligation is that the `habeas-requirements` skill text itself must direct agents to do something. The clause is \"the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to review each group themselves against the review prompt ... one group at a time, before presenting any group to the user.\" A skill that gave different instructions would violate it, and the supplied root is that skill file. The skill is the deliverable, so no code, type or signature obligations exist. `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` covers every element of the clause:\n- Workflow step 3 (`section[Habeas requirements]/section[Workflow]/paragraph@1a08805c21f5`) says \"If you can't start subagents, review each group yourself against the prompt, one group at a time.\" That is the fallback when subagents are unavailable, and the prompt is the `references/review-prompt.md` it names earlier in the same step.\n- Review is step 3 and presenting groups to the user is step 4 (`.../paragraph@7b764a629ec4`), so the review comes before any group is presented.\n\nThe root is therefore adequate for this requirement. Whether the review prompt has the content `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.review_prompt` demands is that requirement's own concern and is not judged here.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has one behavioral obligation. It covers a skill instruction that applies where subagents are unavailable. The instruction must tell agents to review each group themselves against the review prompt, one group at a time, before presenting any group.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_reviews_groups_itself_without_subagents]` checks this against the bundled `habeas-requirements` skill. It uses `step_of`, which panics if no workflow step contains the phrase. The test therefore asserts three things:\n- The skill has a step containing \"If you can't start subagents, review each group yourself against the prompt, one group at a time\". That covers the unavailable-subagents condition, self-review, the review prompt, and the one-group-at-a-time instruction.\n- That step's number is lower than the number of the step containing \"Present each group to the user\". That covers the \"before presenting any group\" ordering.\n- The `SKILL` constant is `habeas-requirements`, so the right skill is checked.\n\nThe prompt's own content belongs to `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.review_prompt`. That requirement is cited here only as context, so it needs no test here.\n\nThe test could miss a skill that contained the phrase in the wrong form. That is a text-matching limit, not a gap in the obligation. A wrong phrase, a missing step, or the wrong order would all fail the test.",
  "references": "809469ff456627f84cc6031d22b8aa563ecb99638f28a287845c6759801b5b11",
